---
/**
 * Full-Mouth Rehabilitation — Vivid Smiles Dentistry, Parker CO.
 *
 * Built from SEO-locked markdown copy (no prototype) using porcelain-veneers
 * as the structural template. Section order
 * mirrors veneers 1:1 with four documented adaptations:
 *
 *   1. #gallery — DROPPED. No service-specific FMR before/after photos exist;
 *      reusing veneer photos would violate the "never fake the categorization"
 *      rule.  (gum-contouring) precedent.
 *   2. #lasting → #cost. Same paper-band 2-col card pattern, but the left
 *      column is a 3-row attribute list (Implants & restoration / Insurance /
 *      Financing) instead of a stat, and the right column carries the closing
 *      "no treatment begins without a clear picture of the plan" prose.
 *   3. #compare → #options as a 2-card grid with the
 *      hybrid path featured. Source copy describes exactly two pathways
 *      (full-arch implants vs. implants + cosmetic), so a 3-card grid would
 *      need invented content.
 *   4. #local → #why-us as a 2x2 .why-4up grid carrying the four "Why Choose
 *      Vivid Smiles for Full-Mouth Rehab?" bullets verbatim. Page-local
 *      pattern; lift to a shared component if a third page adopts it.
 *
 * Imagery reuses photos from elsewhere in src/assets/images/ (services hub +
 * home/) per the precedent — every reuse is marked with a
 * `// TODO: replace with full-mouth-rehabilitation-specific photo` comment so
 * the swap points are greppable when real photography lands.
 *
 * Page-scoped styles: src/styles/pages/full-mouth-rehabilitation.css
 * Buttons + scroll reveals wired by src/scripts/animations.js (data-vs-arrow / data-vs-reveal*).
 *
 * Global <Nav /> + <Footer /> are mounted by BaseLayout — this page renders
 * only its own content, starting with an inline breadcrumb under the global nav.
 *
 * MIGRATED TO BLOCKS (docs/PAGE-BLOCKS.md 2.3). Eight top-level bands — why,
 * what, options, process, design, cost, why-us, faq — each guarded with
 * `hasBlocks ? null : …` and each carrying a row in cms/import/block-map.json
 * under /cosmetic-dentistry/full-mouth-rehabilitation/. No gallery band and no
 * <LocalTrust> on this page, so there is no gallery_marquee row and no
 * code_section row: eight bands, eight blocks, one per `sections` row.
 *
 * THE BAND NAMES IN THE COMMENTS BELOW WERE WRONG AND ARE CORRECTED HERE,
 * because the map's `band` values are read off them. `.section.alt` on THIS
 * page is CHARCOAL (full-mouth-rehabilitation.css:228 ->
 * var(--vs-charcoal-green)) and `.section.dark` is SAGE-PALE (:237 ->
 * var(--vs-sage-pale)). The old comments said "cream" and "sage", which are two
 * different BLOCK_BANDS choices painting two different tokens — copying them
 * into the map would have repainted four of these eight bands.
 *
 * TWO BANDS THIS PAGE OWNS THAT NO REGISTERED LAYOUT REPRODUCES, both recorded
 * as known_gaps on their blocks in the map:
 *   1. `cost` is a `.cost-card` — a two-column card with a `.cost-list` <ul> on
 *      the LEFT and `.cost-body` prose on the right. It is NOT the standalone
 *      <section> around a <PricingTiers> that the `pricing_tiers` layout draws,
 *      and it has no plans, prices or tiers to put in one. It is mapped to
 *      `stat_callout`, which carries every word and none of the geometry.
 *   2. `why-us` is a `.why-4up` 2x2 grid of `.why-4up-card`, whose label is a
 *      `<span class="tag">`. `card_grid` carries the same four cards — and they
 *      are real CMS `cards` rows, group `whyUsCards` — but draws them as
 *      `.why-grid` / `.why-card` with the label in a `<div class="num">`.
 */
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Button from "../../components/Button.astro";
import FinalBand from "../../components/FinalBand.astro";
import VirtualConsult from "../../components/VirtualConsult.astro";
import {
  phoneHref,
  phoneLabel,
  phoneE164,
  bookNowHref,
  addressStreet,
  addressCity,
  addressState,
  addressZip,
} from "../../data/contact";
import "../../styles/pages/full-mouth-rehabilitation.css";

// "What is full-mouth rehabilitation" — a real full-arch restoration on a
// lab model. A prosthesis, not a procedure or a patient: the section defines
// what the treatment produces, and an object carries no outcome claim.
// "Design section" — finished-smile macro in profile.
import { getPageContent, type TocLink } from '../../lib/page-content';
import PageBlocks from '../../blocks/PageBlocks.astro';
// tocLinks, processSteps, faqs are edited in WordPress (Pages -> Full-Mouth Rehabilitation in Parker, CO).
// The shapes are unchanged from the arrays that used to live here, so the
// markup below is untouched.
const { blocks, hasBlocks, tocLinks, processSteps, faqs, section, image, seo } =
  await getPageContent(Astro.url.pathname);


// The four #why-us cards, hardcoded here and ALSO held in the CMS as four
// `cards` rows in group `whyUsCards` — verified live, character-for-character,
// meta/title/body against tag/title/body. This array is the else-branch's copy
// and stays; the block path moves the CMS rows instead, so neither side is
// re-typed. Change one and the two disagree, which is invisible until the
// migration switch flips.
const whyUsCards = [
  {
    tag: "Specialized Training",
    title: "600+ hours of specialized training",
    body: "Dr. Richardson completed 600+ hours of advanced surgical and esthetic coursework and served on staff at Implant Pathway, one of the country's most respected implant education facilities.",
  },
  {
    tag: "In-House Technology",
    title: "Robotic placement and in-house fabrication",
    body: "Robotic technology improves implant precision, and on-site milling and 3D printing allow custom restorations without off-site lab delays.",
  },
  {
    tag: "Phased Coordination",
    title: "Phased coordination, in-house",
    body: "Dr. Richardson sequences the surgical, restorative, and esthetic phases himself; on-site CBCT planning and in-house fabrication keep the plan tight across every visit.",
  },
  {
    tag: "Patient Reputation",
    title: "300+ five-star reviews",
    body: "Consistent outcomes across Parker and Douglas County reflect the genuine care patients experience at every stage of treatment.",
  },
];

/**
 * The "On this page" rail, derived from the blocks themselves (docs/PAGE-BLOCKS.md 1.2).
 *
 * Used only when this page renders from `blocks`. The `toc_links` repeater is
 * eight rows that restate the order of the eight bands below it, so a reorder
 * in wp-admin moves a band and leaves its rail entry pointing at the old
 * neighbour — the single largest way a reorder breaks a link. Reading the
 * anchors off the blocks makes that unrepresentable: there is one ordering and
 * the rail is a projection of it.
 *
 * Three rules, in the order they bite:
 *
 * 1. A blank anchor is skipped. Not tidiness — src/scripts/toc-spy.ts:24 feeds
 *    each rendered href straight to document.querySelector(), and
 *    querySelector("") throws a SyntaxError that kills the whole spy, not just
 *    the one entry. PageBlocks.astro emits no id at all for a blank anchor
 *    (`id={anchor || undefined}`), so there is nothing to link to either.
 * 2. An anchor that is not a valid id selector is skipped for the same reason —
 *    "#3-reasons" is legal HTML and an illegal CSS selector. Dropping one rail
 *    entry costs one link; letting it through costs every link on the page,
 *    plus the mobile pill auto-centering. `why-us` passes: the pattern allows a
 *    hyphen everywhere except the first character.
 * 3. Duplicate anchors follow PageBlocks.astro's dedup exactly, second
 *    occurrence onward suffixed `-2`, `-3`. The counter has to advance on every
 *    non-blank anchor, including blocks with no nav_label, or the rail's idea
 *    of "the second #faq" drifts from the id the renderer actually emitted.
 *
 * A blank nav_label means "leave this block out of the rail" (1.2), which is
 * how a band that should not be navigable opts out. Every one of this page's
 * eight blocks has a `toc_links` row, so the derived rail is all eight, in the
 * same order the repeater already lists them.
 */
const ANCHOR_IS_ID_SELECTOR = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$/;

const anchorsSeen = new Map<string, number>();
// Typed as TocLink[] rather than an equivalent inline shape so the ternary in
// the rail below collapses to one type instead of a union of two array types,
// which TypeScript will not let you call .map() on.
const derivedTocLinks: TocLink[] = [];

for (const block of blocks) {
  // A nested block is drawn INSIDE the band above it, not as a band of its own,
  // so it has no id to link to. Without this the rail emits an entry pointing at
  // an anchor nothing renders — a dead link in the "On this page" list.
  if (block?.nested) continue;

  const anchor = typeof block.anchor === 'string' ? block.anchor.trim() : '';
  if (anchor === '') continue;

  const nth = (anchorsSeen.get(anchor) ?? 0) + 1;
  anchorsSeen.set(anchor, nth);

  const label = typeof block.navLabel === 'string' ? block.navLabel.trim() : '';
  if (label === '') continue;

  if (!ANCHOR_IS_ID_SELECTOR.test(anchor)) {
    console.warn(
      `[blocks] anchor "${anchor}" on ${Astro.url.pathname} cannot be used as a selector — ` +
        `omitting "${label}" from the On this page rail so toc-spy keeps working`,
    );
    continue;
  }

  derivedTocLinks.push({ href: `#${nth > 1 ? `${anchor}-${nth}` : anchor}`, label });
}

---

<BaseLayout
  title={seo.title || "Full-Mouth Rehabilitation in Parker, CO | Vivid Smiles Dentistry"}
  description={seo.description || "Full-mouth rehabilitation in Parker, CO with Dr. Bryce Richardson. Implants, crowns, bridges, veneers, and implant-supported dentures combined into one coordinated plan, with digital smile design preview."}
 noindex={seo.noindex}>
  <div class="fmrehab">

    {/* ---------- BREADCRUMB ---------- */}
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <div class="crumbs-inner">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <a href="/services/">Services</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <a href="/cosmetic-dentistry/">Cosmetic Dentistry</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span class="here">Full-Mouth Rehabilitation</span>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <main id="main">

    {/* ---------- HERO ---------- */}
    <header class="hero" data-vs-reveal-batch>
      <div class="wrap hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">Cosmetic Dentistry · Parker, CO</span>
          <h1 data-vs-reveal-lines>Full-Mouth Rehabilitation in <em>Parker, Colorado</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-sub">
            Full-mouth rehabilitation restores function, health, and appearance across multiple teeth in a single
            coordinated plan. Treatment combines whichever procedures each patient's condition requires: implants,
            crowns, bridges, veneers, or implant-supported dentures. Here is what to expect at Vivid Smiles
            Dentistry in Parker, Colorado.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <Button variant="light" href={bookNowHref} hoverLabel="Let's Talk">Book Online</Button>
            <Button variant="ghost-light" href="#consult" hoverLabel="Get a Video">Free Virtual Consult</Button>
            <div class="ratings">
              <span class="stars" aria-hidden="true">★★★★★</span>
              <span>5.0 · 300+ reviews</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-img" data-vs-parallax data-parallax="-30">
          <Image
            src={image("heroImg").url} width={image("heroImg").width} height={image("heroImg").height}
            alt="Smiling woman photographed at the Vivid Smiles Dentistry office in Parker, CO"
            widths={[600, 900, 1400]}
            sizes="(max-width: 991px) 100vw, 50vw"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    {/* ---------- KEYS — at-a-glance ---------- */}
    <section class="keys" id="keys" aria-label="Full-mouth rehabilitation at a glance" data-vs-reveal-batch>
      <div class="keys-grid">
        <div class="keys-label">At a glance</div>
        <div class="keys-item"><div class="k">3–6 mo</div><div class="v">Typical Timeline</div></div>
        <div class="keys-item"><div class="k">4–6 implants</div><div class="v">Per Arch (Typical)</div></div>
        <div class="keys-item"><div class="k">600+ hrs</div><div class="v">Implant Pathway Training</div></div>
        <div class="keys-item"><div class="k">300+ reviews</div><div class="v">Five-Star Care</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {
      /* ---------- ON-THIS-PAGE TOC ----------
       The rail itself is never a block (spec 7: "Not a block, even though it
       is a band") — only its contents move. Derived from the blocks when they
       are drawing the page, read from the `toc_links` repeater when the
       template is. Same markup either way, which is what lets
       src/scripts/toc-spy.ts go on reading its section list off the rendered
       links without knowing which source produced them. */
    }
    <nav class="toc" id="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <div class="toc-inner">
        <span class="toc-label">On this page</span>
        <div class="toc-scroll">
          <div class="toc-list">
            {(hasBlocks ? derivedTocLinks : tocLinks).map((l) => <a href={l.href}>{l.label}</a>)}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </nav>

    {
      /* ---------- WHY (paper) — Who Needs FMR? ----------

       THE MIGRATION SWITCH (docs/PAGE-BLOCKS.md 2.3) starts here. `hasBlocks`
       means "this build can draw this page from its blocks" — not "WordPress
       sent rows" (src/lib/page-content.ts). When it is true PageBlocks draws
       the eight bands in the order an editor arranged them; when it is false —
       which is every build until the backfill has run, and again the moment an
       editor empties the field — every band below renders exactly as it always
       has.

       Written as one guard per band rather than one guard around all eight on
       purpose, and it is not a style choice. Astro's compressHTML pass treats
       an Astro comment expression differently inside a component slot than at
       element level: wrapping these bands in a Fragment silently drops one
       space at every comment boundary below, and scripts/vr-html.mjs compares
       exact bytes and calls that a difference. A guard sitting exactly where
       its section sat emits byte-identical HTML.

       EVERY top-level band between here and <VirtualConsult> is guarded, and
       every one of them has a row in cms/import/block-map.json. Those two facts
       have to move together: a band that is neither blocked nor guarded renders
       in ADDITION to the block run and lands at the bottom of the page, and a
       band that is guarded with no map row disappears on backfill with nothing
       in the log. There is no third outcome. The bands ABOVE this line — the
       breadcrumb, the hero, `.keys` and the rail — are not blocks by spec 7 and
       are deliberately unguarded, as are <VirtualConsult> and <FinalBand> below
       the run.

       Band colour: `.fmrehab .section` (full-mouth-rehabilitation.css:227) sets
       padding: 110px 0 and nothing else, so the body paper shows through. */
    }
    {hasBlocks ? <PageBlocks blocks={blocks} /> : <section class="section" id="why" data-vs-reveal-batch>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">{section("why").eyebrow}</span>
          <h2><Fragment set:html={section("why").heading} /></h2>
          <p>{section("why").body}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="why-grid">
          <article class="why-card">
            <div class="num">01</div>
            <h3>Damage that compounds</h3>
            <p class="lead">Common scenarios include severe decay, worn teeth from grinding (bruxism), dental trauma, or failing older restorations.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="why-card">
            <div class="num">02</div>
            <h3>Years of compromise</h3>
            <p class="lead">Many have spent years avoiding certain foods or hiding their smile.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>}

    {/* ---------- WHAT (charcoal) — What is FMR? — `.section.alt` is
     var(--vs-charcoal-green) on THIS page (full-mouth-rehabilitation.css:228),
     with h2 #fff at :232 and p rgba(255,255,255,0.85) at :234. NOT the cream
     this comment used to claim and not the cream the identical class name means
     on teeth-whitening.css:237. The map's band value is read off that rule, not
     off the class name. ---------- */}
    {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section alt" id="what" data-vs-reveal-batch>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="what-grid">
          <div class="what-img" data-vs-parallax data-parallax="-25">
            <Image
              src={image("whatImg").url} width={image("whatImg").width} height={image("whatImg").height}
              alt="Full-arch restoration on a dental model, held in a gloved hand"
              widths={[500, 800, 1100]}
              sizes="(max-width: 991px) 100vw, 50vw"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="what-text">
            <span class="eyebrow">{section("what").eyebrow}</span>
            <h2><Fragment set:html={section("what").heading} /></h2>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>{section("what").body}</p>
              <p>
                The procedures vary by case; a plan might include implants, crowns, bridges, veneers, or
                implant-supported dentures based on bone health and tooth structure.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="cta-row left">
              <div class="cta-buttons">
                <Button variant="light" href="#consult" hoverLabel="Get a Video">Free Virtual Consult</Button>
                <Button variant="ghost-light" href="#process" hoverLabel="View Steps">How It Works</Button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>}

    {/* ---------- OPTIONS (paper) — Treatment Options, 2-card compare.
     No background rule on `.fmrehab .section`
     (full-mouth-rehabilitation.css:227), body paper. ---------- */}
    {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section" id="options" data-vs-reveal-batch>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Treatment Options</span>
          <h2><Fragment set:html={section("options").heading} /></h2>
          <p>{section("options").body}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="compare">
          <article class="compare-card">
            <span class="tag">Implant-Supported</span>
            <h3>Dental Implants for Full-Mouth Restoration</h3>
            <p>
              Dental implants replace tooth roots and anchor a permanent foundation for full arch restorations.
              Full arch cases typically use four to six implants per arch, planned with CBCT imaging and placed
              with robotic precision. Dr. Richardson trained at Implant Pathway, one of the country's leading
              implant education facilities.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="compare-card featured">
            <span class="ribbon">Hybrid Plan</span>
            <span class="tag">Implants + Cosmetic</span>
            <h3>Combining Implants with Cosmetic Dentistry</h3>
            <p>
              Patients with some healthy teeth benefit from a hybrid plan: implants for missing teeth, veneers,
              or crowns on natural ones. Digital smile design lets patients preview results before any
              irreversible work begins.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="cta-row">
          <div class="cta-buttons">
            <Button variant="sage" href="#consult" hoverLabel="Get a Video">Free Virtual Consult</Button>
            <Button variant="ghost" href="#faq" hoverLabel="See Answers">Read FAQ</Button>
          </div>
          <span class="cta-note">No commitment · Personal video reply</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>}

    {/* ---------- PROCESS (sage-pale) — `.section.dark` is var(--vs-sage-pale)
     here (full-mouth-rehabilitation.css:237), with h2 var(--vs-ink) at :241.
     PALE, despite the class name, and NOT the `sage` this comment used to
     claim: `sage` and `sage-pale` are two separate BLOCK_BANDS choices painting
     two different tokens. ---------- */}
    {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section dark" id="process" data-vs-reveal-batch>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow light">The Process</span>
          <h2><Fragment set:html={section("process").heading} /></h2>
          <p>{section("process").body}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-grid">
          {processSteps.map((s) => (
            <div class="process-card">
              <span class="step-tag">{s.tag}</span>
              <div class="num">{s.num}</div>
              <h3>{s.title}</h3>
              <p>{s.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="inline-cta dark">
          <div class="ic-text">Ready for the next step? <em>Book online and we'll take it from here.</em></div>
          <div class="ic-buttons">
            <Button variant="light" href={bookNowHref} hoverLabel="Let's Talk">Book Online</Button>
            <Button variant="ghost-light" href={phoneHref} hoverLabel="Tap to Dial">Call {phoneLabel}</Button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>}

    {/* ---------- DESIGN (charcoal) — Digital Smile Design, natural-grid
     pattern. The same `.fmrehab .section.alt { background:
     var(--vs-charcoal-green) }` rule as `what`,
     full-mouth-rehabilitation.css:228. ---------- */}
    {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section alt" id="design" data-vs-reveal-batch>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="natural-grid">
          <div class="natural-text">
            <span class="eyebrow">Treatment Planning</span>
            <h2><Fragment set:html={section("design").heading} /></h2>
            <div class="natural-quote">
              Patients can review and refine before any permanent changes are made.
            </div>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>{section("design").body}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="natural-img" data-vs-parallax data-parallax="-25">
            <Image
              src={image("designImg").url} width={image("designImg").width} height={image("designImg").height}
              alt="Close-up of a smile in profile, photographed against black"
              widths={[500, 800, 1100]}
              sizes="(max-width: 991px) 100vw, 50vw"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>}

    {
      /* ---------- COST (paper) — repurposed lasting-card pattern.
       No background rule on `.fmrehab .section`
       (full-mouth-rehabilitation.css:227), body paper.

       THE BAND NO REGISTERED LAYOUT REPRODUCES, and the one to read the map's
       known_gaps for before reviewing the backfill. `.cost-card`
       (full-mouth-rehabilitation.css:490) is a two-column card: a `.cost-list`
       <ul> on the LEFT, counter-numbered 01/02/03 by
       `.cost-list li::before` (:507), and `.cost-body` prose on the right.

       IT IS NOT A pricing_tiers BAND. That layout draws its own <section>
       around a <PricingTiers> plan grid, which is what the veneers and implant
       pages ship as `<section id="cost">`; this band has no plan, no price and
       no tier to put in one, only three cost FACTORS and two closing sentences.
       Mapping it there would print an empty plan grid and drop every word.

       It is mapped to `stat_callout` instead, which carries every word — the
       three <li> become `points` (lead + body), the two paragraphs become
       `intro` and `intro_2` — and none of the geometry: the card comes back as
       `.lasting-card` / `.lasting-body`, one column, with the list BELOW the
       prose rather than beside it. StatCalloutBlock's own header already names
       `.cost-card` as a Wave C near variant of the shell, which is what closes
       this. Nothing here is a missing FIELD. */
    }
    {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section" id="cost" data-vs-reveal-batch>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">{section("cost").eyebrow}</span>
          <h2><Fragment set:html={section("cost").heading} /></h2>
          <p>{section("cost").body}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="cost-card">
          <div class="cost-list">
            <ul>
              <li>
                <div>
                  <strong>Implants and restoration type</strong>
                  Full arch implant plans differ in cost from hybrid approaches that preserve natural teeth with crowns or veneers.
                </div>
              </li>
              <li>
                <div>
                  <strong>Insurance</strong>
                  Medically necessary components such as extractions or bone grafting may qualify for partial dental or medical benefits.
                </div>
              </li>
              <li>
                <div>
                  <strong>Financing</strong>
                  Third-party financing is available; Vivid Smiles' in-house membership plan also reduces ongoing maintenance costs after treatment.
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="cost-body">
            <p>A consultation with Dr. Richardson includes a full case review and cost estimate.</p>
            <p>No treatment begins without a clear picture of the plan.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>}

    {
      /* ---------- WHY-US (charcoal) — Why Choose Vivid Smiles, why-4up 2x2.
       The same `.fmrehab .section.alt { background: var(--vs-charcoal-green) }`
       rule as `what` and `design`, full-mouth-rehabilitation.css:228 — not the
       cream this comment used to claim.

       THE FOUR CARDS ARE CMS ROWS, not template copy: `cards` group
       `whyUsCards`, four rows, meta/title/body matching the tag/title/body of
       the array in the frontmatter character-for-character. The map MOVES them.

       What the block cannot reproduce is the shell. `.why-4up` (:534) and
       `.why-4up-card` (:538) are page-local classes and the label is a
       `<span class="tag">` (:548); `card_grid` draws `.why-grid` / `.why-card`
       and puts the label in a `<div class="num">`, which this page styles as a
       36px display italic figure (:287). Every word survives, the shell and the
       label's type do not. Recorded on the block in the map. */
    }
    {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section alt" id="why-us" data-vs-reveal-batch>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">{section("why-us").eyebrow}</span>
          <h2><Fragment set:html={section("why-us").heading} /></h2>
          <p>{section("why-us").body}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="why-4up">
          {whyUsCards.map((c) => (
            <article class="why-4up-card">
              <span class="tag">{c.tag}</span>
              <h3>{c.title}</h3>
              <p>{c.body}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>}

    {/* ---------- FAQ (paper) — native details/summary, zero JS. No background
     rule on `.fmrehab .section` (full-mouth-rehabilitation.css:227), body
     paper. ---------- */}
    {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section" id="faq" data-vs-reveal-batch>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">{section("faq").eyebrow}</span>
          <h2><Fragment set:html={section("faq").heading} /></h2>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-list">
          {faqs.map((f) => (
            <details class="faq" open={f.open}>
              <summary><h3>{f.q}</h3><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
              <div class="answer" set:html={f.a} />
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="pull">
          <p>{section("faq").body}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="cta-row">
          <div class="cta-buttons">
            <Button variant="sage" href="#consult" hoverLabel="Get a Video">Still Have Questions? Free Virtual Consult</Button>
            <Button variant="ghost" href={phoneHref} hoverLabel="Tap to Dial">Call {phoneLabel}</Button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>}

    {
      /* ---------- VIRTUAL CONSULT — primary closing conversion.
       NOT a block and deliberately unguarded, like the breadcrumb, hero,
       `.keys` strip and the rail above: it renders on both sides of the switch
       and has no row in the map. It sits after the block run in template order
       and PageBlocks draws at the `why` position, so the closing pair still
       comes last. */
    }
    <VirtualConsult id="consult" eyebrow="Free full-mouth rehab consultation">
      <Fragment slot="headline">Free full-mouth rehab <em>consultation.</em></Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="body">
        Curious about full-mouth rehabilitation? Skip the office visit — Dr. Richardson personally records a
        custom video reviewing your situation, the path that fits your case, and what's possible with implants,
        cosmetic work, or a hybrid plan, all from photos you submit below.
      </Fragment>
    </VirtualConsult>

    {/* ---------- CLOSING BAND ---------- */}
    <FinalBand>
      <p>Vivid Smiles Dentistry in Parker, Colorado, offers the specialized training, technology, and in-house coordination that full-mouth cases require.</p>
    </FinalBand>

    </main>

    <script>
      import { initTocSpy } from "../../scripts/toc-spy";
      initTocSpy(".fmrehab");
    </script>

    {/* JSON-LD structured data — same trio as veneers (MedicalProcedure +
        FAQPage + BreadcrumbList). */}
    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "MedicalProcedure",
      "name": "Full-Mouth Rehabilitation",
      "alternateName": ["Full-Mouth Reconstruction", "Full-Arch Restoration", "Full-Mouth Restoration"],
      "procedureType": "https://schema.org/SurgicalProcedure",
      "bodyLocation": "Mouth",
      "preparation": "Comprehensive exam with CBCT 3D imaging and digital scanning to map bone volume, gum health, and existing restorations before planning begins. Sedation options reviewed; bone grafting may be required prior to implant placement.",
      "howPerformed": "A coordinated, phased plan that may combine dental implants, crowns, bridges, veneers, or implant-supported dentures. Full-arch cases typically use four to six implants per arch, planned with CBCT imaging and placed with robotic precision; hybrid cases combine implants for missing teeth with veneers or crowns on natural teeth, previewed first via digital smile design.",
      "followup": "Phased restoration over three to six months with healing between surgical and restorative phases, followed by ongoing maintenance (routine brushing, flossing, and dental visits; nightguard recommended for bruxism).",
      "performer": {
        "@type": "Dentist",
        "name": "Dr. Bryce Richardson",
        "worksFor": {
          "@type": "Dentist",
          "name": "Vivid Smiles Dentistry",
          "address": {
            "@type": "PostalAddress",
            "streetAddress": addressStreet,
            "addressLocality": addressCity,
            "addressRegion": addressState,
            "postalCode": addressZip,
            "addressCountry": "US"
          },
          "telephone": phoneE164
        }
      }
    })} />

    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": faqs.map((f) => ({
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": f.q,
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a }
      }))
    })} />

    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home",                       "item": new URL("/", Astro.site).href },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Services",                   "item": new URL("/services/", Astro.site).href },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Cosmetic Dentistry",         "item": new URL("/cosmetic-dentistry/", Astro.site).href },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4, "name": "Full-Mouth Rehabilitation",  "item": new URL("/cosmetic-dentistry/full-mouth-rehabilitation/", Astro.site).href }
      ]
    })} />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
